# Valgrind suppressions for ghoti.io-text.
#
# VALGRIND_FLAGS in the Makefile has passed --suppressions=tools/valgrind.supp
# since the file was introduced, and this file has never existed in the
# repository: `tools` was listed in .gitignore, so nothing under it was ever
# committed. Valgrind treats a missing suppressions file as fatal - it prints
# "FATAL: can't open suppressions file" and exits 1 before running anything -
# so `make test-valgrind` and `make test-valgrind-quiet` could not have
# succeeded for anyone, on any machine, in that time.
#
# The set is deliberately empty. Nothing in this library needs suppressing
# today, and an empty file is a valid suppression set, so the flag now names
# something real. Add an entry here only for a leak that is demonstrably not
# ours - one in libc, the dynamic loader, or Google Test - and say in a comment
# which, and why it cannot be fixed on our side.
